              "content": {
                "html": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><strong>Henri Becquerel</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Over a hundred years ago, in early 1896, the French physicist, Henri Becquerel, discovered that a mysterious X-ray was produced by uranium. Becquerel's achievement was itself based on the work of the German scientist, Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen, who had discovered X-rays only a few months earlier in November 1895</span></p>",
                "colorRole": "default"
              },
              "groupId": null,
